<% content_for :title, "On Anger | Bipolar Sober" %>

<style>
  .anger-page {
    background: #080808;
    color: #fff;
    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
  }

  .anger-page *,
  .anger-page *::before,
  .anger-page *::after {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  .anger-hero {
    min-height: 85vh;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 80px 6%;
    background-color: #080808;
    background-image:
      linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(8, 8, 8, .55), transparent),
      url("<%= asset_path('bipolar_anger_desktop.png') %>");
    background-size: cover;
    background-position: center;
  }

  .anger-hero-content {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .anger-eyebrow {
    max-width: 440px;
    margin: 0 0 28px;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.6;
    letter-spacing: .12em;
  }

  .anger-hero h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(72px, 10vw, 150px);
    font-weight: 900;
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: .88;
    letter-spacing: -.065em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .anger-hero h1 span {
    display: block;
  }

  .anger-intro {
    margin: 32px 0 0;
    font-size: clamp(15px, 1.6vw, 22px);
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .anger-quote {
    padding: 48px 6%;
    background: #080808;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .anger-quote blockquote {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .anger-quote blockquote p {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    color: #eaff00;
    font-size: clamp(30px, 5vw, 64px);
    font-weight: 900;
    font-style: italic;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .anger-quote cite {
    font-size: 14px;
    font-style: normal;
  }

  .anger-section {
    padding: 72px 6%;
  }

  .anger-section-inner {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, .85fr) minmax(0, 1.15fr);
    gap: 60px;
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .anger-number {
    margin: 0 0 22px;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: .12em;
  }

  .anger-section h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(36px, 4.5vw, 68px);
    font-weight: 900;
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: .95;
    letter-spacing: -.045em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .anger-copy {
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .anger-copy p {
    margin: 0 0 22px;
  }

  .anger-copy p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .anger-copy ul {
    margin: 0 0 24px;
    padding-left: 22px;
  }

  .anger-copy li {
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .anger-pink {
    background: #ff1493;
    color: #080808;
  }

  .anger-yellow {
    background: #eaff00;
    color: #080808;
  }

  .anger-purple {
    background: #8a00ff;
    color: #fff;
  }

  .anger-black {
    background: #080808;
    color: #fff;
  }

  .anger-white {
    background: #fff;
    color: #080808;
  }

  .anger-takeaway {
    padding-top: 22px;
    border-top: 3px solid currentColor;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .anger-footer {
    padding: 40px 6%;
    border-top: 1px solid #444;
  }

  .anger-footer-inner {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 24px;
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .anger-footer a {
    color: #eaff00;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.5;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .anger-footer a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .anger-footer a:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid #ff1493;
    outline-offset: 6px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .anger-hero {
      min-height: 88svh;
      align-items: flex-start;
      padding: 48px 6% 60px;
      background-image:
        url("<%= asset_path('bipolar_anger_mobile.png') %>");
      background-position: center bottom;
    }

    .anger-eyebrow {
      margin-bottom: 24px;
      font-size: 10px;
    }

    .anger-hero h1 {
      font-size: clamp(64px, 19vw, 108px);
    }

    .anger-intro {
      margin-top: 24px;
      font-size: 14px;
    }

    .anger-section {
      padding: 48px 6%;
    }

    .anger-section-inner {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 28px;
    }

    .anger-section h2 {
      font-size: clamp(36px, 10vw, 58px);
    }

    .anger-copy {
      font-size: 16px;
      line-height: 1.8;
    }

    .anger-number {
      margin-bottom: 16px;
    }
  }
</style>

<main class="anger-page">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="anger-hero" aria-labelledby="anger-title">
    <div class="anger-hero-content">

      <p class="anger-eyebrow">
        BIPOLAR SOBER / BIPOLAR / ANGER
      </p>

      <h1 id="anger-title">
        <span>ON</span>
        <span>ANGER.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="anger-intro">
        THE SHORT FUSE.<br>
        THE FULL-BODY FUCK THIS.<br>
        THE SPACE BEFORE YOU REACT.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- QUOTE -->
  <section class="anger-quote" aria-label="Opening quote">
    <blockquote>
      <p>“Serenity now!”</p>
      <cite>— Frank Costanza</cite>
    </blockquote>
  </section>


  <!-- 01 / BIPOLAR RAGE -->
  <section class="anger-section anger-pink">
    <div class="anger-section-inner">

      <div class="anger-section-heading">
        <p class="anger-number">01 / BIPOLAR RAGE</p>

        <h2>
          ONE MORE<br>
          FUCKING<br>
          THING.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="anger-copy">
        <p>
          Traffic won’t move. Your computer freezes. You drop something
          when your back already hurts. One small inconvenience suddenly
          feels unbearable. Then you get angry at yourself for getting
          so angry, and now you have two things to be pissed off about.
        </p>

        <p>
          “Bipolar rage” describes overwhelming anger or irritability;
          it is not a separate diagnosis. Irritability can occur during
          mood episodes, but anger alone does not mean you are having one.
          Having bipolar disorder does not make you inherently aggressive.
          Pay attention to the intensity and the broader pattern.
        </p>

        <p>
          Your jaw clenches. Your hands tighten. Everything demands an
          immediate reaction. Recognizing that your response feels bigger
          than the situation can help you pause. Turning that awareness
          into another reason to hate yourself only adds pressure.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 02 / THOUGHTS -->
  <section class="anger-section anger-yellow">
    <div class="anger-section-inner">

      <div class="anger-section-heading">
        <p class="anger-number">02 / CHECK THE STORY</p>

        <h2>
          A FROZEN<br>
          SCREEN.<br>
          A WHOLE<br>
          SPIRAL.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="anger-copy">
        <p>
          One problem can collect every other problem you have been
          carrying. A lost document becomes “nothing ever works.”
          An unfinished chore becomes “I can’t manage my life.”
          Pain interrupts your day, and suddenly you are reliving
          everything your body has kept you from doing.
        </p>

        <p>
          Come back to the specific event. What happened? What are you
          predicting? What judgment did you add? “I lost my work and need
          to redo it” is frustrating enough without becoming
          “I’m a fucking failure.”
        </p>

        <p class="anger-takeaway">
          You can recognize anger, tension, and the urge to act without
          treating that urge as an instruction.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 03 / RESPONDING -->
  <section class="anger-section anger-purple">
    <div class="anger-section-inner">

      <div class="anger-section-heading">
        <p class="anger-number">03 / WORK WITH WHAT IS</p>

        <h2>
          WHAT CAN<br>
          YOU DO<br>
          WITH THIS?
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="anger-copy">
        <p>
          Try treating the inconvenience as a challenge to your
          resourcefulness. Given that this happened, what response
          would help? A delay asks for patience. A broken plan asks
          for improvisation. A mistake asks for repair.
        </p>

        <p>
          You do not have to enjoy it or believe it happened for a reason.
          Give your attention something useful to do beyond listing
          how unfair everything is. Success might mean leaving the task
          alone for ten minutes instead of breaking something you will
          have to replace.
        </p>

        <p>
          You cannot force traffic to move or guarantee your body will
          cooperate. Ask, “What can I do with things as they are?”
          Your effort still matters when the outcome disappoints you.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 04 / THE PAUSE -->
  <section class="anger-section anger-black">
    <div class="anger-section-inner">

      <div class="anger-section-heading">
        <p class="anger-number">04 / BEFORE YOU REACT</p>

        <h2>
          PUT THE<br>
          FUCKING<br>
          THING<br>
          DOWN.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="anger-copy">
        <p>
          When your body is highly activated, complicated reflection
          can wait. Stop, step back, and observe before proceeding.
          Set down the object. Stop typing. Pause the task.
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>Name what is happening: “I’m angry and I want to react.”</li>
          <li>Give yourself time without rehearsing the grievance.</li>
          <li>Ask what will leave you with fewer problems an hour from now.</li>
          <li>Get support when you cannot settle enough to respond safely.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          On the road, prioritize safe driving over recovering lost time.
          Loosen your grip, leave space, and let a missed turn stay missed
          until you can change direction safely. If you are too overwhelmed
          to drive safely, pull over somewhere safe.
        </p>

        <p class="anger-takeaway">
          You can be late and still have handled the situation well.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 05 / SELF-DIRECTED ANGER -->
  <section class="anger-section anger-white">
    <div class="anger-section-inner">

      <div class="anger-section-heading">
        <p class="anger-number">05 / ANGRY AT YOURSELF</p>

        <h2>
          OWN IT.<br>
          REPAIR IT.<br>
          KEEP YOUR<br>
          DIGNITY.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="anger-copy">
        <p>
          Later, get curious about what the anger is protecting.
          Helplessness? Fear of losing control? Exhaustion from pain?
          Explore without forcing an explanation. You can listen to
          the angry part while also listening to the parts that want
          safety, sobriety, and stability.
        </p>

        <p>
          Calling yourself stupid will not restore lost money or undo
          a decision. Name what happened accurately, address what you can,
          and consider what would help next time: a reminder, a limit,
          an earlier break, or another person’s support.
        </p>

        <p class="anger-takeaway">
          Your mistakes need attention. You remain worthy of care
          while addressing them.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 06 / COMMISERATING -->
  <section class="anger-section anger-pink">
    <div class="anger-section-inner">

      <div class="anger-section-heading">
        <p class="anger-number">06 / ANGER CAN SPREAD</p>

        <h2>
          VENTING.<br>
          OR ADDING<br>
          FUEL?
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="anger-copy">
        <p>
          Someone agrees that your situation is bullshit, you remember
          another grievance, and soon you are taking turns getting
          each other more furious. It feels validating. Check what
          happens afterward: do you feel supported and more able
          to cope, or more ready to explode?
        </p>

        <p>
          Commiserating can help you feel less alone. Repeatedly
          replaying the same grievance can also keep you stuck in it.
          Agreement may feel like proof while you reinforce each
          other’s assumptions.
        </p>

        <p>
          Try saying, “I need to vent for a few minutes, then help me
          figure out what to do.” Compassion can acknowledge how
          shitty something is and help you find a way forward.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- 07 / THE BIGGER PATTERN -->
  <section class="anger-section anger-yellow">
    <div class="anger-section-inner">

      <div class="anger-section-heading">
        <p class="anger-number">07 / PROTECT YOUR PROGRESS</p>

        <h2>
          THE PAUSE<br>
          COUNTS.
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="anger-copy">
        <p>
          If anger is unusual for you or comes with changes in sleep,
          energy, thoughts, or behavior, bring it to your treatment team.
          Coping skills and reflection can support you. Some symptoms
          need more help than your usual strategies can provide.
        </p>

        <p>
          You will not handle every frustration gracefully. Notice
          the reckless move you do not make, the object you put down,
          and the mistake you address without spending the evening
          hating yourself.
        </p>

        <p class="anger-takeaway">
          Those responses count. You are learning to experience anger
          while protecting the life you are working to build.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- NAVIGATION -->
  <nav class="anger-footer" aria-label="Bipolar topic navigation">
    <div class="anger-footer-inner">
      <%= link_to "← BACK TO BIPOLAR", bipolar_path %>
      <%= link_to "NEXT: ON MANIA →", bipolar_mania_path %>
    </div>
  </nav>

</main>